
### Email change links on Lambda

The email change sends a link to the new address and a notice to the old one through `deliverLink` (`packages/auth/src/link-delivery.ts`), which only logs them until a mailer is plugged in. A Lambda gives the request no `waitUntil` and freezes the process when the handler returns, so the auth route (`handleAuthRequest` in `apps/web/src/lib/auth/auth.ts`) holds its answer until the deliveries of the request are done, and none is lost. The cost is a timing difference: once a real mailer is plugged in, a request for an address that has an account answers later than one for an address that has not (nothing is sent for it), by the time the mailer takes. A mailer that answers in milliseconds narrows the gap; handing the link to a queue (SQS, ...) instead of sending it closes it.
